				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">My friends, it has come to war.
<br />

<br />
The Albion King, Arthur Pendragon, so wise above his own people, has died. The peace that his rule inspired has died with him. Previously, the treaties between the three realms of Albion, Midgard, and our fair Hibernia, forged by King Arthur, had kept the barbarian hordes from assaulting our lands. They did not taint Hibernia, nor did we humble them with our presence in their lands. Now they press upon our borders, hungry for conquest. We Undermountain Folk of the Elves and Lurikeen sensed this change, and have returned from beyond the Veil. We found the two halves of Men we left behind, the Celts and the giantesque Firbolg, still tending Hibernia. We had come to defend Hibernia against the zealots of Albion and the savages of Midgard, yet the Undermountain Folk found strife within our own borders. Some Celt and Firbolg raised voice and even weapon at the Folk, claiming we had abandoned Hibernia, and it was theirs. They became sore afraid at us, such creatures of magic and thought that they could not comprehend. Some Folk began to return this in word and deed, thinking the Men-races beneath them, and they fought, forgetting the reason we had returned from the Veil.
<br />

<br />
The strife must end.
<br />

<br />
Now that the enemy is at our gates, pounding upon our doors and calling for our blood, we must stand united. In ignorance the Men-races of Hibernia saw us Undermountain Folk as a threat, and in ignorance the Folk saw these Celts and Firbolg as the same. But are we so blind as to not see the true threat? Celt and Firbolg, Elf and Lurikeen, we are all sons and daughters of Hibernia. Our enemies will surely plunder the magics of our land if we cannot come to realize this. That is the purpose of Evoluxa, set upon by its founding members of all races. We must teach order through unity, and we shall forge all our peoples into a great sword that will be thrust deep into the belly of the beasts that would see our home defiled.
<br />

<br />
We are a family. Each of us is brother or sister to the other. And we are not ignorant of what it is to be a family. We give unto each other what may be needed. We rally to defend a brother or sister when under attack. We make an example to all our realm-mates. We may find rare occasion to fight amongst even ourselves, but we know that each of us truly respects the other, or we would not be a family.
<br />

<br />
Like a family, we shall have levels of responsibility to help oversee the practices of Evoluxa. Those who desire admittance to the guild shall seek out the Dia Armpala, who is the officer charged with recruitment. It is their task to become acquainted with each petitioner, and then with the whole of Evoluxa, decide upon their membership. Upon first joining the guild, the rank of Initiate will be granted, and for a period of time their compatibility shall be evaluated. Successful passage through Initiate rank shall earn the rank of Privatus, which all members of Evoluxa carry with pride.
<br />

<br />
Two other officer positions exist. The Dia Chixom is responsible for all events, raids, and campaigns that Evoluxa may officially sponsor. The Dia Sepia shall be our communications officer, seeing that lines of dialogue exist both within the guild, and to the other guilds of Hibernia. The supreme commander of Evoluxa is known as the Chancellor, and it is them who is the final representative of the guild. Each officer may, as need arises, nominate an il-Khan to be their assistant, to support the officer’s duties.
<br />

<br />
Both strength and flexibility are the hallmarks of true rule, and thus as time flows and changes, this Charter may change with it. We operate by the spirit of this Charter. All our rules and practices may not be specifically scribed therein, but know that they follow the spirit of this document, for rules need only be written to enforce actions and thoughts not already present in our hearts and minds. May the fair realm of Hibernia be bound in unity, vanquish their foes, and endure forever.
<br />

<br />
Set by my hand this day,
<br />

<br />
Taeloth Siannodel, Mentalist of Tír na nÓg</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
